    "body": "[A10] Second evidence addendum for R519-2-F1 / R519-3. The head is unchanged at `c4539ff1`.\n\n`review-evidence/pp163-r1/author-r3/measurement-m3final/inputs-digest/` (archive `90f80dda`) now holds:\n- **`inputs-components.json`.** It lists the gate's 124 file components in script order: name, path (roots and host prefixes replaced), whether the file is normalized, and `sha256`. It also lists the generics. The manager replayed `pp_resource_gate.inputs()` on the measurement directory and got the recorded `24ba6a24\u2026` exactly.\n- **`inputs/`.** These are the four inputs that are not in the processor tree, so each can be hashed directly:\n  - `Ram_1w_1rs_Generic.v` and `Ram_1w_1ra_Generic.v` (components 117 and 118);\n  - the VexiiRiscv LiteX netlist (119);\n  - the generated integrated top in the normalized form the gate hashes, `alinx_ax7101.normalized.v` (120: comments removed, roots replaced; it contains no host path).\n- **`replay_inputs.py` and `baseline_images.json`.** The script chains the components, generics and images. It prints `24ba6a24\u2026 match`.\n\nEvery other component can be recomputed from this head's sources and the include headers. R519-4 will verify this.",
